course: dictionary
lesson: 5232
title: Words about people and groups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a kind of person, and the words around them tell you what kind. «The Italian Jesuit Matteo Ricci lived in China from 1582 to 1610.» Italian tells you where he came from, and lived in China tells you where he went. Jesuit sits between them, so it must name a kind of person.
explain: The sentence also says he «mastered Chinese» and «made a world map in Chinese». Those clues show a learned person who studied hard. Ask yourself: what would fit in the gap? Then check your guess against the other clues in the sentence.
explain: Capital letters give clues too. Jesuit starts with a capital J, so it names a particular group, not just any person. When a word is new, use the clues first, then a dictionary to confirm.
fact: A Jesuit is a member of the Society of Jesus, a Roman Catholic group of priests and brothers.
fact: Saint Ignatius of Loyola founded the Society of Jesus in 1540.
fact: Jesuits are known for their schools and universities, their missions around the world and their work in science.
fact: Pope Francis was a Jesuit, and many schools in the USA, Ireland and Australia are Jesuit schools.
fact: In the past, «jesuitical» was used as an unfair insult for someone thought to be sly in an argument.
exercise: «The Italian Jesuit Matteo Ricci lived in China from 1582 to 1610.» What kind of person is a Jesuit? | *A member of a Roman Catholic group of priests and brothers | A stage magician who performs tricks | A ruler of a country in the past | A kind of sailing ship
exercise: Which saint founded the Society of Jesus in 1540? | *Saint Ignatius of Loyola | Matteo Ricci | Pope Francis | Saint Francis
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Many schools in Ireland are Jesuit schools.» What does Jesuit school probably mean? | A school with no teachers | *A school run by Jesuits | A school that teaches only maths | A school for sailors only
test: «He mastered Chinese and made a world map in Chinese.» What do these clues suggest about Matteo Ricci? | *He was clever and studied hard | He was a sailor who never learned to read | He was a farmer who never left Italy | He was a king who ruled China
test: Where was Matteo Ricci buried, with the emperor's permission? | Rome | *Beijing | Sydney | Dublin
exam: In one sentence, what is a Jesuit? | *A member of the Society of Jesus, a Roman Catholic group of priests and brothers | A king in an old story | A person who builds bridges | A kind of fish
